// heart_beat is an apply too, even though the driver dispatches it by a
// cached index (prog->heart_beat) rather than by name -- so it is not in the
// master-applies table that the dispatch cache uses, and it had to be added
// to the object half of vm/internal/applies for the compiler to see it.
//
// It is the worst apply to make async, not the most obscure: the driver
// discards the return value, so a rejection has no handler at all, and the
// beat re-fires every tick while the previous one is still parked -- one more
// suspended frame per beat, against `max suspended async functions`.
async void heart_beat() {}
